<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">World Health Organization</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1948</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as WHO</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The World Health Organization is the specialised agency of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> for international public health, founded on 7 April 1948 with its headquarters in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a>. It sets health standards, coordinates responses to epidemics and supports national health systems. Its campaigns led to the eradication of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smallpox">smallpox</a>, declared in 1980, and it coordinated the international response to the COVID-19 pandemic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/world-health-organization.jpg" alt="World Health Organization" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guilhem Vellut from Annecy, France · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:World_Health_Organization_@_Pregny-Chamb%C3%A9sy_(50636746028).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
